\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 When visualizing a new indicator, identify the database and follow these specific steps:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 1. ACS (e.g., Rent Burden)
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Acquire:
\f1\b0  Update \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 USER_VARIABLES_NEEDED\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  with the new variable (e.g., \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 RENTGRS\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ).\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Prepare:
\f1\b0  Update \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 USER_INDICATOR_NAME\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 . In Section 2.4, write logic for \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 indicator_to_plot\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  (e.g., \cf3 \cb4 \strokec3 if_else(RENTGRS > 30, 1, 0)\cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ).\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
